# Final empirical sweep for ComPort loopback echo
# After factory reset, with chassis in clean state
# Chassis responds to UpdateRequest on 29 permanent CIDs with slot-level
# identity responses, but silently drops ComPort write dispatches.

=== Fingerprint of all 29 CIDs ===
Group 0 (15 CIDs): 0x0101, 0x0103-0x010A, 0x0133-0x0138
  Template: 03 00 | 08 0e 09 38 00 10 18 26 | 03 16
Group 1 (14 CIDs): 0x0139-0x013A, 0x0153,55,57,59, 0x0183-0x018A
  Template: 03 00 | 08 0e 09 39 00 10 18 26 | 03 16

All 29 CIDs are same-type services (just two sub-groups by response).
No unique "DmMd dispatcher" CID stands out from fingerprinting.

=== Final write sweep (per fork recommendation) ===
7 representative CIDs x 2 leaf types (0x15 serial-15 and 0x34 serial-34)
x 30 join numbers (1-30) = 420 ComPort write attempts total.
Payload: 'PING\r' as StringInput to each.

RESULT: Zero PING loopback echoes received.
RESULT: Zero response frames of any kind on ComPort writes
        (writes are silently accepted by the chassis TCP but not
         dispatched to the DM-link RMC).

The RMC's TX->RX physical loopback is wired and known-working from
prior IPID 1 masquerade sessions. The chassis's OEM program is
accepting our frames at the TCP layer but is NOT routing them to
the DM-link endpoint stack. Confirmed empirically on fully-reset
chassis state.
